  "preamble": "In Lithuanian the Proto-Balto-Slavic diphthong *ai became the diphthong ie in much of the lexicon: *snáigas 'snow' > sniegas, *aiˀnas 'one' > vienas. Inherited *ei gave the same ie (dievas 'god'), so the two diphthongs merged. Related forms such as snaigė 'snowflake' keep the older ai.",
